From 4a53032b64af3bfd9ed158b5bde074196866b046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Feb 2026 14:36:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Allow fingerprint HAL to read serialno_prop

GrapheneOS restricts access to serialno_prop to a small set of domains
as a privacy hardening measure. However, many vendor fingerprint HALs
read the device serial number to bind fingerprint templates to the
specific device. Without this access, the HAL's TEE commands fail
during enrollment because the TA cannot identify the device.

Add hal_fingerprint_server to the neverallow exception list so the
fingerprint HAL can read the serial number property.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000013
---
 private/domain.te | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/private/domain.te b/private/domain.te
index 77097d2..ea0206d 100644
--- a/private/domain.te
+++ b/private/domain.te
@@ -870,6 +870,7 @@ neverallow {
   -hal_camera_server
   -hal_cas_server
   -hal_drm_server
+  -hal_fingerprint_server
   -hal_keymint_server
   userdebug_or_eng(`-incidentd')
   -init
-- 
2.52.0

